            title: "Handling Cycles",
            concept: "Cycles keep reference counts above zero even when the whole group is unreachable, so a collector needs cycle detection or a tracing pass to reclaim them. Mark-and-sweep handles cycles naturally because it only follows reachability from the roots.",
            syntax: "/* cycle: a -> b -> a */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int total = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) total += i;\n    printf(\"total: %d\\n\", total);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
